Z||000000||p-man||01-18-2001||02:30 PM||||3400 tdc has 10 more HP and a higher red line.But the 3800 naturally aspirated motor makes  torque than the 3400. which is the better motor.i guess the 3400 tdc would beat the in something past the 1/4 mile but would get dogged by the 3800 in the1/4. 3400 has multi- cams.and the 3800 has 4 bolt main cross drilled. and comes with roller rockers. which motor would be better stock for stock. and which motor is the best when modified and cheaper performance parts.please give me your input on this subject||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||01-18-2001||02:45 PM||||Sounds like you have all the pros and cons filled in already. It purely depends on where your preferences lie.  Kind of like a Coke vs Pepsi type of thing.<P> My personal preference would go with the 3.8, as it is a very reliable powerplant (had an Olds Ciera 3.8 with over 112k miles, ran like a champ) and is very torquey. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||01-18-2001||08:27 PM||||Hands down the 3800 is more reliable, cheaper, and there is more performance parts available. I would go for the supercharged 3800 engine if I were you. It makes 240 horsepower in stock form and 280 horsepower with just a pulley change. <P>Here is a place you can get performance parts for the 3800 and 3.8-liter engines. <A HREF="http://www.thrasher-ep.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.thrasher-ep.com</A>  <P>||||reg||1
